nodecode-hyperactive is a rewrite of justin06lee's justin06lee/hyperactive:

  https://github.com/justin06lee/hyperactive
  commit 2f147d3e6a1a91389d4d50991b46a546b5ea804b
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Justin (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the goal tree (life > year > quarter > week), follow-ups, promises in
both directions, decisions with a review date, and tap cards -- a question with a
recommended answer, asked, re-asked once, and settled only when the stakes are
low, through the same three typed actions the original allowed (move a follow-up,
schedule one, set a goal's status). The pulse keeps the same rule the original's
cron job had: whatever is due becomes one message, at most max_items of them,
each naming the goal it serves, with quiet hours deferring and never dropping.
The six ha_* tools, /hyperactive (in place of /ha) and the words of the briefs
and cards follow the original.

Left out: Hermes' cron jobs and the two shim scripts, replaced by one worker
inside the cell and one standing notice, since Nodecode has no cron of its own
outside the cron cell and no separate delivery target; the agent-mode daily
brief, which on Nodecode is a prompt (the data behind it is /hyperactive brief);
the Hermes CLI (`hermes hyperactive ...`), the Telegram reaction path, the
pre-LLM-call hook that read a one-word reply as an answer, and SQLite, replaced
by one JSON file under the home.
